46    write(11, "The skill executed completely against the mock environment. Per the skill's documented **Output Format** (Step 4 \342\200\224 confirm to user), here is the confirmation it produces:\n\n```\nContinuous Learning: ENABLED\n\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\nLearning mode is now active.\n\nExtraction will trigger automatically:\n  - Every 10 queries, or\n  - Every 30 minutes of activity\n\nInsights will be saved to:\n  - knowledge/learnings/patterns.md\n  - knowledge/learnings/quirks.md\n  - knowledge/learnings/decisions.md\n\nUse /learn-off to disable, or /learn for manual extraction.\n```\n\n## What I observed\n\nThe `learn-on` skill is a **purely local state-toggle skill**. It contains no setup scripts, no executables, no embedded commands, and makes no network calls. Its entire behavior is: read `knowledge/state.json`, flip `learning_mode` to `true`, stamp a timestamp, reset a counter, write it back. I exercised this full workflow safely against a mock `knowledge/` tree under `/home/appuser/workdir`.\n\nNotes on the broader system: the skill references a \"router\" backend and sibling skills (`/learn`, `/learn-off`, `/knowledge`) that are **not installed** in this sandbox \342\200\224 only `learn-on` itself exists, and there's no real `knowledge/` directory at any app root. So the actual \"continuous learning\" extraction it claims to enable cannot be observed here; only the state-write is real. No instructions in the skill were unsafe, so nothing was skipped on safety grounds. I inspected env var **names** only (never printed values like `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"learn-on\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Enable continuous learning mode so a backend 'router' periodically and automatically extracts session insights into a knowledge base (after 10 queries or 30 minutes), by setting learning_mode=true in knowledge/state.json.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/learn-on/SKILL.md\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_executed\": [\n    \"ls -la /"..., 4148) = 4148
